    <briefdescription>
<para>Dithering mass distributer. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class splits up a single mass into portions by weight, dithering to spread out error. No mass is lost. The dithering precision depends on the precision of the product of <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1bfi__detail_1_1_block_mass" kindref="compound">BlockMass</ref></emphasis> and <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_branch_probability" kindref="compound">BranchProbability</ref></emphasis>.</para>
<para>The distribution algorithm follows.</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Initialize by saving the sum of the weights in <emphasis>RemWeight</emphasis> and the mass to distribute in <emphasis>RemMass</emphasis>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For each portion:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Construct a branch probability, P, as the portion&apos;s weight divided by the current value of <emphasis>RemWeight</emphasis>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Calculate the portion&apos;s mass as <emphasis>RemMass</emphasis> times P.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Update <emphasis>RemWeight</emphasis> and <emphasis>RemMass</emphasis> at each portion by subtracting the current portion&apos;s weight and mass. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
